WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.288
One rule ties the data and
network layers together:

2
00:00:03.288 --> 00:00:07.450
match each flow's consistency needs
to the transport built for it.

3
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:10.673
Strongly consistent
writes and their quorum

4
00:00:10.673 --> 00:00:13.388
stay inside one region, on the fast path.

5
00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:18.212
Everything that crosses regions is
asynchronous and rides the bulk path.

6
00:00:18.212 --> 00:00:21.587
That's not a limitation; it's
using physics on purpose.

7
00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:26.491
The program's own SaaS data plane is
the worked example: one regional writer

8
00:00:26.491 --> 00:00:31.712
and tokens on both sides, so SD-WAN would
matter only for background replication.

9
00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:33.580
Now the same rule at a branch.
